{# The single footer action bar of a screen or a form (design_campus_manager README 8a/8b): a
   faint line of context on the left, the buttons pushed to the right.

   <twig:Cm:ActionBar :lastModified="quizTemplate">
       <twig:Cm:Button variant="primary" type="submit">Enregistrer</twig:Cm:Button>
   </twig:Cm:ActionBar>

   The content is the buttons. The `meta` block is the line on the left; `lastModified` (an
   entity using AuditableTrait) fills it with « Modifié le … par … » instead - and only once a real
   edit has happened: lastUpdatedDate stays null until then, and there is nothing honest to claim
   about a last modification before one exists. #}
{% props lastModified = null %}
{% set meta %}{% block meta %}{% endblock %}{% endset %}
{% if meta|trim is empty and lastModified and lastModified.lastUpdatedDate %}
    {% set meta = 'lastModifiedByMetaLabel'|trans({'%date%': lastModified.lastUpdatedDate|date('d/m/Y'), '%name%': lastModified.lastUpdatedBy.displayName ?? lastModified.lastUpdatedBy.username}) %}
{% endif %}
<div{{ attributes.defaults({class: 'cm-actionbar'}) }}>
    {% if meta|trim is not empty %}
        <span class="cm-actionbar__meta">{{ meta }}</span>
    {% endif %}
    <div class="cm-actionbar__buttons">
        {% block content %}{% endblock %}
    </div>
</div>
